The Ampere frontend as seedds/nxnative has it on branch oot-wip @ ee9b7765d579c46e45a7297493565e098f3bda33 (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 seedds; https://github.com/seedds/nxnative): Decoders/AmpereOp.cs, DecoderAmpere.cs, Instructions/InstEmitAmpere.cs,
InstEmitAmpereAlu.cs, InstEmitAmpereMem.cs, InstEmitAmpereTensor.cs, Transforms/TensorPass.cs as of that commit and the
Ampere part of Translator.cs (EmitOpsAmpere: guarded deferred writes, no fall-through with writes pending). Against
patch 0017 this adds what nxnative did after MacNativeGames' port, among it: bindless and uniform-register texture
forms (TEX / TLD / TLD4 / TXD / TXQ 0x361, 0x364, 0x367, 0x370, 0xf60, 0xf63, 0xf6c), surface reductions (0x59f),
ATOMS.CAS, F2I.U64 / I2F from 64 bits, FLO, HMUL2 .H0_NH1, LDC .IS banks, the separate texture and sampler entries of
an NVN2 compute c[0] (67f1d00552564f818e4f9577cb98d9d5d80d5f36), image and buffer handles in uniform buffers and guarded
Ampere loads (9507c221c8138e10f647313196409c793d24a35c), TXD through a uniform register
(f9b438fbac1e3a07508171c2412f1b203c3d28b3), .FTZ comparisons on Ampere (84dea69835414b18a4351cd45054bb611e0e3185),
BMSK and 0x925 (7bccfc88a4f2e93a2d225c9d91c0e3ee44ade4d2), and the task / mesh stage memory (0x927, ISBERD modes).
Shared pieces taken with it, none of which changes a Maxwell translation: IoVariable.HelperInvocation appended (IoMap
entries), InstEmitAluHelper.FlushDenormal (only Ampere calls it: nxnative 84dea69's Maxwell FSET / FSETP / FCMP change
is not taken), EmitLoadConstant's optional banks, InstEmitSurface's optional cbufSlot for atomics on handles in uniform
buffers, IGpuAccessor.QueryAmpereStageMemory and RecordTexelFetch1D (default no-ops). nxnative's other shared changes
(BindlessElimination table handles, BindlessToArray bases, Maxwell TLDS 1D wrap, PIXLD) are not taken.
Patch 0022 adapts parts of it to Vulkan.

